#X obj 230 78 cnv 1 535 240 empty empty empty 17 7 0 10 -237178 -1 0;
#X text 240 83 the object routes bang messages to the first outlet
and all other messages (floats \, symbols \, lists \, any) to the second
outlet;
#X text 240 138 by default an empty list is treated as a bang. Set
@strict to true to disable this behavior and route empty lists to the
second outlet;
#X text 240 193 to get properties \, use the [prop.get] object \, since
all messages (including property requests) are passed through;
#X text 240 248 the object can be used to separate bangs from other
messages \, for example to trigger an action only on a bang and ignore
floats or symbols;
